{"name":"Windows 10 support cliff for NovaSeq 6000 control PCs: Illumina knowledge-base pages, follow-on upgrade bulletins, and lab or core IT notices","url":"https://knowledge.illumina.com/instrumentation/general/instrumentation-general-reference_material-list/000009668","access":"Opened the page with WebFetch; no login needed. It lists the NovaSeq 6000 on Windows 10 LTSB 1607, with extended support 'through October 13, 2026', or on LTSC 1809, supported to 9 Jan 2029. Illumina 'does not support' Windows 11 and 'will provide more information in the future' on OS upgrades. The page carries no date. Next steps: (1) Open https://knowledge.illumina.com/instrumentation/general/instrumentation-general-faq-list/000006353 (control-software 30.0.C06 runs the 1607 build; 30.1.C01 runs 1809) and https://emea.support.illumina.com/support-content/windows10.html, plus FAQ 000002247. (2) Search: \"NovaSeq 6000\" \"LTSC\" upgrade; \"NovaSeq 6000\" \"1607\" OR \"LTSB\" core facility; \"NovaSeq 6000\" \"operating system\" upgrade fee OR \"field service\" 2026; site:.edu \"NovaSeq 6000\" \"Windows 10\". (3) Look for hospital IT and NHS DSPT 'unsupported OS' exception registers that name sequencers (search: \"unsupported operating system\" sequencer NHS Illumina).","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"This is a forced decision point the street hasn't priced in. Any 6000 still on the 1607 build loses Microsoft extended support on 13 Oct 2026, the day after today. Clinical labs under HIPAA, CAP or NHS cyber rules must then patch, isolate or replace the machine. It matters what Illumina does next. A paid OS-upgrade or service-plan requirement would show whether Illumina is lengthening the tail (inelastic, 'permanent') or pushing migration. Either way, it dates when the tail must act, which could be 2027. Clinical 6000 owners keeping the machines would also show low elasticity.","expected_payoff":"high"},
{"name":"SEC EDGAR full-text search sweep: which filers still name the NovaSeq 6000 versus the NovaSeq X (2023 to 2026, all forms)","url":"https://efts.sec.gov/LATEST/search-index?q=%22NovaSeq%206000%22&dateRange=custom&startdt=2025-07-01&enddt=2026-10-12&forms=10-K,10-Q","access":"Tested with WebFetch; no login needed. For 10-K and 10-Q filings dated 1 Jul 2025 to 12 Oct 2026, the query \"NovaSeq 6000\" returned only 1 hit: Caris 10-K (3 Mar 2026). Re-run by year: 2023, 2024, 2025 and 2026, with no forms filter (to include S-1, 8-K Ex.99, DEF 14A and 424B) and for each of \"NovaSeq 6000\", \"NovaSeq X\" and \"NovaSeq\" plus \"transition\". The \"NovaSeq X\" query with no forms filter returned HTTP 500, so retry with &forms=10-K,10-Q,S-1,8-K or a narrower date window. The browser UI is https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/#/q=%22NovaSeq%20X%22 . Record each filer, date and sentence (quotes of 15 words or fewer).","labels":["1A","1C"],"rationale":"Counting filers that name each platform each year is a cheap way to see where small and mid-cap clinical customers stand (CareDx, Castle, Biodesix, Sera, Bionano, Personalis, Exagen and others), beyond the big labs already read. Labs that drop the 6000 from their risk factors or COGS text have converted. Filers that keep naming it, or describe revalidation costs, are the inelastic tail. The first test shows only Caris naming the 6000 in periodic filings since mid-2025, which itself hints that most named customers have moved.","expected_payoff":"medium"},
{"name":"Japan PMDA package-insert (添付文書) revision history for cancer genomic profiling tests: does the regulated Japanese tail name the NovaSeq 6000 or the X?","url":"https://www.pmda.go.jp/PmdaSearch/kikiDetail/GeneralList/23000BZX00403000_1_01","access":"Seen in search results; not opened. The PMDA list page for FoundationOne CDx (approval 23000BZX00403000) shows a partial-change approval (一部変更承認) PDF dated 7 Oct 2025. Older insert versions are at https://www.pmda.go.jp/PmdaSearch/kikiDetail/OldPdfData/23000BZX00403000_1_01/16 (try indices 1 to 16). Also check 30300BZX00074000 (another CGP program), FoundationOne Liquid CDx, Guardant360 CDx (Japan), GenMineTOP and OncoGuide NCC Oncopanel by searching PMDA kiki for 遺伝子変異解析プログラム(がんゲノムプロファイリング検査用). In each PDF, search for NovaSeq, シーケンサー and 使用機器, and note the version date. The PDFs may be compressed; if so, extract them locally with pdftotext.","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"This tests the regulated-tail claim outside the US (FDA, IVDR and NY routes are already covered). If Japanese approvals still name only the 6000 in 2025–26, the regulated tail is sticky across jurisdictions, which cuts against our 2027 conversion. A partial change that adds the NovaSeq X would show labs paying the regulatory cost to move, which supports conversion. Insert versions are dated, which gives a clock.","expected_payoff":"medium"},
{"name":"Census of used NovaSeq 6000 dealer and surplus listings and asking prices (EquipNet, SSLLC, Reuzeit, MSU Surplus Store, Exapro, LabExchange, Labprocure)","url":"https://www.equipnet.com/illumina-novaseq-6000-sequencing-system-listid-1083249/","access":"Search-result snippets showed: EquipNet listings 1083249 (2021 unit) and 1083377 (2022 unit) at $20,000 each; Reuzeit https://reuzeit.com/product/3374237-illumina-novaseq-6000-dna-sequencing-system-great-condition at $5,699 (was $19,000) and /product/3376672 at $200,000 with S4 buffers; MSU Surplus https://msusurplusstore.com/products/illumina-novaseq-sequencing-system at $60,000; SSLLC A203796, A203799 and A117632; Exapro p241113061. Open each page and record list date, year of manufacture, seller type (university surplus, closed company, broker) and price. Compare with Illumina's $985K US list price (15 Feb 2024 Open Offer disclosure). Search for more with site:equipnet.com \"NovaSeq 6000\", site:ssllc.com NovaSeq, and \"NovaSeq 6000\" auction 2026 (Heritage Global, BioSurplus, Federal Equipment).","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"Units built in 2021–22, now worth $5.7–60K (99% below list), point to a glut from decommissioned machines. Counting the 2026 listings and their sources gives a supply-side estimate of the retirement pace, which Illumina stopped disclosing after Q4'25. A rising count of clinical-company or hospital sellers would mean the clinical tail is shrinking. Very low prices also mean cheap spare parts, which could prolong the inelastic tail: a watch-out that cuts both ways.","expected_payoff":"medium"},
{"name":"Non-US listed clinical labs' exchange filings and press releases on the 6000→X move and cost per test (India NSE/BSE: Dr Lal PathLabs, Metropolis, Agilus; Korea DART: GC Genome, Green Cross; Japan TDnet: H.U. Group/BML)","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/LALPATHLAB_25062025112327_FINALPressRelease25062025.pdf","access":"Seen in search results; not opened. The Dr Lal PathLabs NSE filing (25 Jun 2025) appeared in a NovaSeq X search, and Agilus installed an X (biospectrumindia.com/news/16/27246). Open the PDF, then search nsearchives.nseindia.com and bseindia.com for 'NovaSeq'. Korea: dart.fss.or.kr full-text search for 'NovaSeq' (GC Genome 사업보고서). Japan: search \"NovaSeq X\" 導入 検査 2026 site:co.jp. Extract the platform named, the timing, and any per-test cost or capacity claim.","labels":["1A","1C"],"rationale":"Large clinical labs outside the US that disclose to exchanges are a sample of the clinical 6000 tail that nobody has checked. A filing that says they will keep the 6000 for legacy assays supports the 'permanent tail' view. One that says they will retire it and cut cost per test by X% supports more conversion in 2027 and gives an elasticity read (cost saved versus volume added).","expected_payoff":"medium"},
{"name":"CAP Today annual NGS-instrument product guide: Illumina entries with US installed units and list prices (unverified field)","url":"https://www.captodayonline.com/product/illumina-7/","access":"The URL came up in search; not opened, and I could not confirm that the guide has an installed-units field. Open it, then search site:captodayonline.com \"NovaSeq 6000\" and site:captodayonline.com \"product guide\" sequencing instruments, for each year 2022–2026. If the guide gives 'units installed in US' or 'units sold in the past year' by model, transcribe the series for the 6000 versus the X.","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"A clinical-lab trade guide filled in by the vendor could carry a dated US installed-base or list-price figure for the 6000 by year. That would replace the base disclosure Illumina stopped after Q4'25. The payoff is uncertain until the fields are confirmed.","expected_payoff":"low"}
